1
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:18,420
Aiming for the sunset floating
over the Nakagawa River,

2
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:23,560
I kick a pebble and it flies until it goes,

3
00:00:24,420 --> 00:00:29,340
we were talking on the
way home from gym class,

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,800
they laughed that I was still
full of energy just as I was.

5
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:37,440
Even if I stir up some energy somewhere,

6
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:38,680
Gutsy, there's no other way.

7
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:41,940
A nightmare, the unchanging streetscape

8
00:00:41,940 --> 00:00:43,880
is gentler than ever.

9
00:00:44,720 --> 00:00:46,860
Because the crows are cawing,

10
00:00:46,860 --> 00:00:48,700
the sun has already set.

11
00:00:49,720 --> 00:00:53,900
Are the yakitori stalls really there?

12
00:00:54,900 --> 00:00:57,460
Of the pointed hat,

13
00:00:57,460 --> 00:01:02,420
from the waterworks on toward the big ruler,

14
00:01:02,420 --> 00:01:04,080
the sunset falls.

15
00:01:06,680 --> 00:01:10,080
Tomorrow too,
I'll drop it and it'll end, won't it?

16
00:01:10,080 --> 00:01:12,740
Maybe a magazine, saying happiness again,

17
00:01:12,740 --> 00:01:14,660
I realized it only after losing it.

18
00:01:14,660 --> 00:01:16,280
Because I'm a fool.

19
00:01:17,280 --> 00:01:19,740
Yeah!

20
00:01:25,200 --> 00:01:27,040
Little Ryo-chan

21
00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:32,440
Come on, throw the ball over here!

22
00:01:32,580 --> 00:01:33,360
Over here, over here!

23
00:01:33,660 --> 00:01:35,860
Which way, which way?

24
00:01:36,220 --> 00:01:36,840
Go for it!

25
00:01:39,460 --> 00:01:41,926
I envy them.
If only I could become a kid again,

26
00:01:41,976 --> 00:01:44,660
I'd love to run wild and
play to my heart's content.

27
00:01:47,280 --> 00:01:48,640
Hey! Ryo-su!

28
00:01:49,100 --> 00:01:50,200
Aaah! Chief!

29
00:01:50,700 --> 00:01:52,420
I wasn't slacking off or anything!

30
00:01:52,720 --> 00:01:55,500
I was just thinking about the state of
the world and the peace of the nation!

31
00:01:55,540 --> 00:01:58,420
Did you really think I'd
fall for such an obvious lie?

32
00:01:58,520 --> 00:01:59,640
You blockhead!

33
00:02:00,020 --> 00:02:03,280
If you're going to goof off here,
I'll dock your pay!

34
00:02:03,820 --> 00:02:05,720
Get back to work already!

35
00:02:06,060 --> 00:02:06,600
Yes, sir!

36
00:02:06,600 --> 00:02:08,600
Iiiiiii

37
00:02:10,020 --> 00:02:10,600
Hey,

38
00:02:10,600 --> 00:02:11,980
Hey,

39
00:02:11,980 --> 00:02:12,300
Hey,

40
00:02:13,680 --> 00:02:16,240
I got all heated up
from running so suddenly.

41
00:02:16,240 --> 00:02:17,380
I can't take it anymore.

42
00:02:19,460 --> 00:02:20,560
Go for it!

43
00:02:20,560 --> 00:02:21,720
Go for it!

44
00:02:25,580 --> 00:02:26,800
Kids

45
00:02:26,800 --> 00:02:28,800
Lucky kids.

46
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:30,540
They've got plenty of stuff to play with,

47
00:02:30,540 --> 00:02:32,600
and no annoying bosses.

48
00:02:32,600 --> 00:02:34,780
For someone like you, there's Rokon...

49
00:02:36,600 --> 00:02:38,620
Esaki! Don't just barge in like that!

50
00:02:38,940 --> 00:02:40,720
Now, now, calm down.

51
00:02:41,120 --> 00:02:43,780
Getting angry so easily is
proof you're short on calcium.

52
00:02:44,200 --> 00:02:46,960
Eat some of these dried
sardines and get your calcium.

53
00:02:47,420 --> 00:02:48,640
Mind your own business!

54
00:02:48,960 --> 00:02:51,600
So? What's tonight, then?

55
00:02:52,020 --> 00:02:53,620
A useless invention, is it?

56
00:02:54,280 --> 00:02:57,920
You could say this one
was born just for you.

57
00:02:58,220 --> 00:03:01,880
It's a groundbreaking, magnificent
invention that will go down in human history.

58
00:03:02,400 --> 00:03:06,280
Do you have any idea how much
effort it took to develop this?

59
00:03:06,280 --> 00:03:08,860
Skip the preamble and just show it to me.

60
00:03:09,280 --> 00:03:12,180
Fine, then this time's invention is

61
00:03:13,040 --> 00:03:14,040
Kametta

62
00:03:14,040 --> 00:03:16,920
A hard candy?

63
00:03:16,920 --> 00:03:21,260
If I may put it in a way that sounds
totally with-it and youthful, candy!

64
00:03:21,700 --> 00:03:25,020
This is a super groundbreaking
and super amazing invention,

65
00:03:25,020 --> 00:03:28,400
Never mind that.
What happens if you eat that candy?

66
00:03:29,640 --> 00:03:31,560
Seeing is believing.

67
00:03:31,880 --> 00:03:33,360
Ha-ha-ha!

68
00:03:34,200 --> 00:03:35,960
Just look at this.

69
00:03:35,960 --> 00:03:39,280
Ha-ha-ha!

70
00:03:39,280 --> 00:03:43,220
Ha-ha-ha!

71
00:03:43,220 --> 00:03:45,560
Ha-ha-ha!

72
00:03:45,560 --> 00:03:50,120
Ha-ha-ha!

73
00:03:50,120 --> 00:03:50,160
Ha-ha-ha!

74
00:03:50,160 --> 00:03:50,300
Ha-ha-ha!

75
00:03:50,300 --> 00:03:50,620
Ha-ha-ha!

76
00:03:50,620 --> 00:03:51,660
Ha ha

77
00:03:51,660 --> 00:03:55,880
Ha ha

78
00:03:55,880 --> 00:04:01,860
Ha ha

79
00:04:02,400 --> 00:04:03,840
I-I've turned into an egg!

80
00:04:04,480 --> 00:04:05,560
Now do you understand?

81
00:04:06,100 --> 00:04:09,500
This candy can make
whoever licks it younger!

82
00:04:10,920 --> 00:04:13,600
So if an adult human eats it...

83
00:04:13,600 --> 00:04:16,864
Precisely, they become children.
How about that? This is exactly

84
00:04:16,914 --> 00:04:19,940
Th-this is a revolutionary invention!

85
00:04:20,500 --> 00:04:22,380
Give it, give it, give me that candy too!

86
00:04:22,960 --> 00:04:26,482
Very well.
This invention is for adults like you.

87
00:04:26,532 --> 00:04:28,120
Go ahead and lick it, don't hold back.

88
00:04:31,820 --> 00:04:34,300
With this, I too can become a child again

89
00:04:46,960 --> 00:04:48,440
We've turned into kids!

90
00:04:49,440 --> 00:04:50,480
Of course.

91
00:04:50,480 --> 00:04:52,560
My invention is perfect.

92
00:04:54,600 --> 00:04:57,520
I'm going to enjoy being
a kid to the fullest!

93
00:04:58,120 --> 00:04:59,900
Ahaha, that's the one!

94
00:05:00,260 --> 00:05:02,080
Hey, let me join in too!

95
00:05:06,360 --> 00:05:07,580
Who are you?

96
00:05:07,800 --> 00:05:08,800
It's fine, it's fine.

97
00:05:09,360 --> 00:05:10,180
Here we go!

98
00:05:16,760 --> 00:05:17,820
Wow!

99
00:05:18,140 --> 00:05:19,480
I've never seen anything like that.

100
00:05:21,340 --> 00:05:23,380
Alright, let's go again!

101
00:05:26,660 --> 00:05:29,840
Since we're kids,
free rides on trains and buses are OK.

102
00:05:29,840 --> 00:05:31,040
Long live kids!

103
00:05:35,620 --> 00:05:39,260
Since we're kids, sweets are OK too, right?

104
00:05:53,820 --> 00:05:54,680
Eeeeeeh!

105
00:05:58,560 --> 00:06:03,420
Life without work or nagging
bosses is the best! Woohoo!

106
00:06:04,740 --> 00:06:10,420
Ryo-san, what the hell! That idiot
still hasn't come back to the police box?

107
00:06:11,960 --> 00:06:18,100
What's got you so worked up?
Didn't you see Ryotsu Kankichi?

108
00:06:18,780 --> 00:06:22,100
Senpai? No, I didn't see him.

109
00:06:22,100 --> 00:06:25,380
Where is that good-for-nothing
slacking off now?

110
00:06:25,380 --> 00:06:29,000
It can't be helped, Chief.
He's Ryo-san, after all.

111
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:29,360
What?

112
00:06:29,960 --> 00:06:30,880
That's right.

113
00:06:30,880 --> 00:06:33,720
So no matter what you say to a useless person,
it's useless.

114
00:06:34,840 --> 00:06:38,540
Senpai's uselessness is hardcore, after all.

115
00:06:38,540 --> 00:06:41,000
Let's just give up on Senpai.

116
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:44,600
Now that you mention it, you're right.

117
00:06:45,080 --> 00:06:46,720
Guess we'll just let it go.

118
00:06:48,440 --> 00:06:51,640
Chief, I bought some delicious manju.

119
00:06:51,640 --> 00:06:55,040
There are only five,
so let's eat them without telling Ryo-san.

120
00:06:55,780 --> 00:06:57,500
That sounds great.

121
00:06:57,500 --> 00:06:59,720
Then I'll make some tea.

122
00:07:00,920 --> 00:07:02,564
Those guys...

123
00:07:02,614 --> 00:07:05,520
Don't think you're getting away with this.

124
00:07:06,960 --> 00:07:10,600
Excuse me, one kake soba, please.

125
00:07:10,600 --> 00:07:12,920
A special tempura soba and inari sushi.

126
00:07:13,920 --> 00:07:15,540
And three croquettes.

127
00:07:20,680 --> 00:07:22,020
That was delicious.

128
00:07:22,500 --> 00:07:23,600
Hey, Daddy.

129
00:07:23,600 --> 00:07:24,820
Oh, right.

130
00:07:24,820 --> 00:07:28,120
Up we go, bye-bye.

131
00:07:33,160 --> 00:07:35,620
Thanks for the meal over here too.
The check, please.

132
00:07:35,620 --> 00:07:38,440
Coming right up. That's 1,060 yen in total.

133
00:07:38,440 --> 00:07:40,200
Did you raise the prices?

134
00:07:40,200 --> 00:07:40,817
No,

135
00:07:40,867 --> 00:07:45,540
plain soba is 260 yen and the
special tempura soba is 380 yen.

136
00:07:45,700 --> 00:07:47,220
Make it inari sushi and a croquette.

137
00:07:47,440 --> 00:07:50,500
Hey, wait a second.
Why are you ordering for that kid too?

138
00:07:51,100 --> 00:07:53,800
What are you talking about?
That's the customer's child, isn't it?

139
00:07:54,340 --> 00:07:54,740
Yeah.

140
00:07:56,280 --> 00:08:00,220
Hehehe, I'm so satisfied, so satisfied.

141
00:08:01,040 --> 00:08:03,940
Alright, the rest of the gang,
let's keep this up.

142
00:08:03,940 --> 00:08:04,180
Zaaah!

143
00:08:04,180 --> 00:08:05,480
Yay!

144
00:08:07,680 --> 00:08:10,300
Ohh, what a predicament.

145
00:08:11,800 --> 00:08:37,500


146
00:08:37,500 --> 00:08:40,680
The frog's, the edge of the
rim is slimy and wiggling around!

147
00:08:44,140 --> 00:08:45,740
Oh my, what's wrong? Little boy...

148
00:08:52,960 --> 00:08:53,980
What are you doing?

149
00:08:55,600 --> 00:08:57,600
Hurry up and open the cart ball,
I'm telling you!

150
00:08:59,620 --> 00:09:00,940
No, come on!

151
00:09:05,180 --> 00:09:05,980
That was fun.

152
00:09:07,500 --> 00:09:09,140
Nice! Being a kid is the best!

153
00:09:19,360 --> 00:09:21,100
A seesaw spin!

154
00:09:21,620 --> 00:09:22,520
Alright!

155
00:09:27,200 --> 00:09:30,540
Yes, yes, little boy.
Children aren't allowed in here, you know.

156
00:09:30,760 --> 00:09:34,620
Hey! I'm not a child! I'm...

157
00:09:34,620 --> 00:09:37,620
Oh right, I'm a child right now, aren't I.

158
00:09:38,140 --> 00:09:39,177
Which means,

159
00:09:39,227 --> 00:09:43,760
If I don't turn back into an adult, does that
mean no booze or pachinko for the rest of my life?

160
00:09:45,240 --> 00:09:47,680
Being a kid is more
inconvenient than I thought.

161
00:09:47,680 --> 00:09:49,280
Found them.

162
00:09:51,460 --> 00:09:54,940
Hey, little guy, where are you from?

163
00:09:55,120 --> 00:09:57,080
Could you come with us to the police box?

164
00:09:57,500 --> 00:09:59,460
There's nothing to be scared of.

165
00:10:03,520 --> 00:10:03,840
I see.

166
00:10:05,240 --> 00:10:08,640
So everyone suffered because
of this child's pranks.

167
00:10:10,760 --> 00:10:13,580
For a kid,
those are pretty old-man-style pranks.

168
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:16,260
They're the kind of harassment
someone like Ryotsu would pull.

169
00:10:17,420 --> 00:10:18,840
So, what's your name?

170
00:10:19,580 --> 00:10:20,220
Well...

171
00:10:22,100 --> 00:10:24,720
Actually,
my dad and mom are both busy with work,

172
00:10:24,720 --> 00:10:27,020
and they've gone far away
and haven't come back.

173
00:10:27,700 --> 00:10:28,020
Oh my.

174
00:10:29,460 --> 00:10:33,180
I was lonely, so I did those things.
I'm really sorry.

175
00:10:35,500 --> 00:10:38,960
It's okay.
I didn't know you had such circumstances.

176
00:10:39,160 --> 00:10:42,340
I'm sorry.
I couldn't understand how you felt.

177
00:10:42,820 --> 00:10:45,380
I'm not fit to be a cop. I'm pathetic.

178
00:10:46,080 --> 00:10:49,218
A complete success.
These guys are all suckers.

179
00:10:49,268 --> 00:10:51,500
I'm a sucker for stories like this.

180
00:10:52,040 --> 00:10:53,100
Alright, I get it.

181
00:10:53,880 --> 00:10:57,420
Until your dads come back,
let's look after you at the police box.

182
00:10:58,380 --> 00:11:00,400
Yeah, let's do that.

183
00:11:00,400 --> 00:11:02,180
Now you won't be lonely anymore.

184
00:11:02,180 --> 00:11:04,280
We're here with you, big sisters are here.

185
00:11:04,840 --> 00:11:06,740
But what about at night?

186
00:11:08,180 --> 00:11:10,320
Then I'll take him home with me tonight.

187
00:11:10,320 --> 00:11:13,560
What are you talking about?
I'm the one who'll take care of this boy.

188
00:11:13,560 --> 00:11:15,140
No, it's me.

189
00:11:15,580 --> 00:11:19,380
You? Think of me as your mom,
and feel free to lean on me.

190
00:11:19,380 --> 00:11:20,620
Me?

191
00:11:20,720 --> 00:11:21,940
No, I'll do it.

192
00:11:22,740 --> 00:11:25,020
Then why don't you just
take turns looking after him?

193
00:11:25,020 --> 00:11:31,260
I see, as expected of the Chief. These two
are just too softhearted for their own good.

194
00:11:31,260 --> 00:11:32,460
Mm.

195
00:11:32,460 --> 00:11:33,660
Mm.

196
00:11:34,600 --> 00:11:35,280
Mm.

197
00:11:36,620 --> 00:11:37,300
me

198
00:11:38,800 --> 00:11:39,480
me

199
00:11:41,720 --> 00:11:42,400
me

200
00:11:42,400 --> 00:11:43,440
me

201
00:11:43,440 --> 00:11:44,180
me

202
00:11:44,180 --> 00:11:44,460
me

203
00:11:49,500 --> 00:11:50,720
Boo-boo!

204
00:11:52,160 --> 00:11:58,480
Looks like we're in this together today It's a cramped room, but I won't let you feel lonely.
Yeah, yeah.

205
00:11:59,960 --> 00:12:03,220
Why do we have to go back
to Nikoniko-ryō again?

206
00:12:07,980 --> 00:12:12,260
Hey, you're speeding right in front of me?
You've got some nerve, don't you?

207
00:12:20,460 --> 00:12:21,900
Stop, stop, is that okay?

208
00:12:21,900 --> 00:12:23,060
Please stop.

209
00:12:28,040 --> 00:12:30,900
Well, in the end we ended up all
the way out to the Bōsō Peninsula.

210
00:12:30,900 --> 00:12:36,240
Sorry, when I spot a speeding violation,
my body just moves on its own.

211
00:12:36,240 --> 00:12:37,520
Poor thing.

212
00:12:38,240 --> 00:12:40,220
Then let's go to my place tonight.

213
00:12:40,220 --> 00:12:41,840
Really? Yes!

214
00:12:45,600 --> 00:12:46,840
W-what is this?

215
00:12:50,060 --> 00:12:51,040
It's over around there.

216
00:12:55,400 --> 00:12:56,820
It's ridiculously big, isn't it.

217
00:12:57,560 --> 00:12:58,840
It's for our health.

218
00:12:59,300 --> 00:13:02,340
If we keep relying on convenient
things like cars and planes,

219
00:13:02,340 --> 00:13:04,460
our bodies will go soft.

220
00:13:05,180 --> 00:13:06,080
N-no way.

221
00:13:07,520 --> 00:13:08,300
We're running.

222
00:13:08,300 --> 00:13:11,360
Come on,
let's work up a refreshing sweat together!

223
00:13:12,420 --> 00:13:13,140
Hey, wait!

224
00:13:13,140 --> 00:13:14,280
Hey, wait up!

225
00:13:14,680 --> 00:13:16,560
I'm gonna beat five hours today.

226
00:13:16,560 --> 00:13:17,540
Five hours?

227
00:13:18,940 --> 00:13:20,340
The wind feels great.

228
00:13:27,020 --> 00:13:27,940
That's impossible.

229
00:13:31,260 --> 00:13:33,820
Kei-chan, you can't be serious.
That's impossible.

230
00:13:33,820 --> 00:13:35,160
He's just a child.

231
00:13:36,400 --> 00:13:39,040
I've gotten used to it, so I didn't notice.

232
00:13:39,540 --> 00:13:40,580
I'm reflecting on what I did.

233
00:13:40,580 --> 00:13:42,280
I can't take it anymore.

234
00:13:42,280 --> 00:13:44,480
I want to live in a normal house.

235
00:13:45,120 --> 00:13:47,020
Then it's our turn tonight.

236
00:13:48,740 --> 00:13:50,860
It's a normal house, so don't worry.

237
00:13:51,720 --> 00:13:52,200
Haah...

238
00:13:56,140 --> 00:13:58,900
A-are you okay? Watch your step.

239
00:13:59,800 --> 00:14:01,500
That's my line.

240
00:14:01,500 --> 00:14:02,800
Who's that? Don't eat that!

241
00:14:03,240 --> 00:14:05,000
Please mind the doors as they open.

242
00:14:06,280 --> 00:14:08,940
It gets a bit crowded from this station,
so bear with it.

243
00:14:08,940 --> 00:14:11,640
What? Then what was it until now?

244
00:14:11,740 --> 00:14:13,820
Can this thing even fit any more people?!

245
00:14:20,340 --> 00:14:24,000
I'm used to it now,
but it must've been rough on the kids

246
00:14:24,680 --> 00:14:27,380
Looks like it's just me here, after all.

247
00:14:28,280 --> 00:14:30,820
Let's go to big sis's
place from today, okay?

248
00:14:33,380 --> 00:14:35,920
Looks like we can finally take it easy.

249
00:14:40,720 --> 00:14:41,380
Whoa!

250
00:14:42,760 --> 00:14:44,340
It's a normal room!

251
00:14:45,600 --> 00:14:47,100
Feel free to use anything, okay?

252
00:14:48,740 --> 00:14:49,700
Don't hesitate to say so.

253
00:14:50,420 --> 00:14:51,860
Yes, understood.

254
00:14:53,280 --> 00:14:53,880
Alright!

255
00:14:55,080 --> 00:14:57,820
Here, we can live the good
life to our heart's content.

256
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:04,620
Hey, you're heavy!

257
00:15:04,620 --> 00:15:05,420
Get off me!

258
00:15:08,240 --> 00:15:09,280
We've been spotted.

259
00:15:09,280 --> 00:15:10,380
Sera.

260
00:15:10,380 --> 00:15:11,740
Were you hiding there?

261
00:15:13,240 --> 00:15:14,820
Sera's gotten so excited.

262
00:15:14,820 --> 00:15:17,040
She's happy to have made friends, isn't she?

263
00:15:18,920 --> 00:15:22,740
Come on, Sera!
I'll leave the rest to you! Wait a minute!

264
00:15:23,560 --> 00:15:23,980
Mm?

265
00:15:28,920 --> 00:15:49,440
Uuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuu

266
00:15:49,440 --> 00:15:59,440
But I wonder... if things stay like this, that kid will end up alone again.
Well then, starting today, you should come stay at our house, okay?

267
00:15:59,440 --> 00:16:04,720
No, I must respectfully decline.
Oh my, you know such difficult words!

268
00:16:07,240 --> 00:16:15,700
I've been wondering this whole time... I feel like I've seen that face somewhere.
What are you talking about, mister?

269
00:16:15,700 --> 00:16:17,120
You're imagining things.

270
00:16:18,120 --> 00:16:18,820
I see.

271
00:16:21,600 --> 00:16:23,660
As expected of the Chief, you're sharp.

272
00:16:23,660 --> 00:16:26,460
We have to be careful
not to let anything slip.

273
00:16:27,620 --> 00:16:28,320
We're home.

274
00:16:29,500 --> 00:16:30,860
Excuse us.

275
00:16:30,860 --> 00:16:32,140
Welcome.

276
00:16:32,140 --> 00:16:34,120
The room is all ready for you.

277
00:16:34,120 --> 00:16:35,580
Make yourselves at home.

278
00:16:35,580 --> 00:16:36,200
Yes.

279
00:16:42,740 --> 00:16:45,000
Now, eat plenty!

280
00:16:45,700 --> 00:16:46,480
Hey, this looks delicious!

281
00:16:47,680 --> 00:16:48,560
Thanks for the food.

282
00:16:50,260 --> 00:16:52,260
Home cooking really is the best!

283
00:16:55,800 --> 00:16:57,100
Ma'am, seconds, please.

284
00:16:57,300 --> 00:16:58,740
Ahaha.

285
00:17:05,140 --> 00:17:05,980
Morning.

286
00:17:06,160 --> 00:17:07,020
Good morning.

287
00:17:07,460 --> 00:17:09,020
How's that kid doing?

288
00:17:09,220 --> 00:17:10,540
He's still asleep.

289
00:17:10,680 --> 00:17:11,140
What?

290
00:17:16,640 --> 00:17:17,560
Wake up.

291
00:17:19,700 --> 00:17:20,740
What?

292
00:17:20,740 --> 00:17:23,280
Kids should go to bed
early and get up early.

293
00:17:23,280 --> 00:17:24,980
We're starting radio calisthenics!

294
00:17:26,860 --> 00:17:29,020
One, two, three, four.

295
00:17:29,020 --> 00:17:31,140
Come on, put more energy into it!

296
00:17:32,100 --> 00:17:34,440
One, two, three, four.

297
00:17:35,840 --> 00:17:38,700
Why do I have to do this?

298
00:17:39,820 --> 00:17:40,820
Itadakimasu.

299
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:43,520
Bakabon!

300
00:17:44,420 --> 00:17:48,560
You're supposed to put your hands together and say
"itadakimasu" before a meal, aren't you?

301
00:17:48,560 --> 00:17:50,200
Sorry.

302
00:17:53,580 --> 00:17:54,780
Don't be a nuisance.

303
00:17:54,780 --> 00:17:56,300
Your manners are terrible.

304
00:17:56,300 --> 00:17:56,960
Yes.

305
00:18:04,480 --> 00:18:05,540
Bakabōn!

306
00:18:06,560 --> 00:18:08,180
Your chopstick technique is terrible.

307
00:18:08,180 --> 00:18:10,300
Start practicing properly from today.

308
00:18:10,760 --> 00:18:11,160
Yes.

309
00:18:11,160 --> 00:18:11,420
Yes!

310
00:18:12,540 --> 00:18:14,300
I'm a guest here, you know!

311
00:18:14,560 --> 00:18:15,680
Did you say something?

312
00:18:15,860 --> 00:18:17,020
N-no…

313
00:18:19,580 --> 00:18:21,100
Bakamōn!

314
00:18:21,860 --> 00:18:24,160
Is there anyone who lounges
around in the middle of the day?!

315
00:18:24,300 --> 00:18:26,620
Kids should be outside
playing energetically!

316
00:18:26,740 --> 00:18:27,460
Y-yes, sir!

317
00:18:29,880 --> 00:18:32,000
That's why I hated going
to the Chief's house!

318
00:18:35,620 --> 00:18:37,400
I see, as expected of you, Chief.

319
00:18:37,400 --> 00:18:39,120
Isn't that a bit too harsh?

320
00:18:39,900 --> 00:18:43,500
Not just a little, I hate it.
I don't want to go back to that house.

321
00:18:44,560 --> 00:18:46,380
Right, time to head home.

322
00:18:46,380 --> 00:18:47,120
Gulp!

323
00:18:47,120 --> 00:18:49,000
Well, today, that's...

324
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:51,880
Stop mumbling and let's go!

325
00:18:51,880 --> 00:18:54,120
Aw, no way!

326
00:18:55,960 --> 00:18:57,680
It's the master.

327
00:19:04,360 --> 00:19:07,900
Thinking about what's waiting
at home makes me so depressed.

328
00:19:14,140 --> 00:19:16,900
So a new one came in?

329
00:19:16,900 --> 00:19:18,740
I've got to go buy one right away.

330
00:19:19,400 --> 00:19:21,680
I'm broke right now.

331
00:19:29,720 --> 00:19:31,320
Dinner's ready!

332
00:19:32,640 --> 00:19:34,080
I'm starving.

333
00:19:39,040 --> 00:19:40,000
Thank you for the meal.

334
00:19:41,120 --> 00:19:41,800
Thank you for the meal.

335
00:19:42,760 --> 00:19:44,840
Well, go ahead and eat up.

336
00:19:44,840 --> 00:19:45,580
Y-yes.

337
00:19:48,620 --> 00:19:50,140
How does it taste? Is it good?

338
00:19:50,140 --> 00:19:51,320
Yes, ma'am.

339
00:19:51,320 --> 00:19:52,860
Good, good.

340
00:19:52,860 --> 00:19:54,540
Well, keep eating, don't hold back.

341
00:19:54,540 --> 00:19:56,600
And don't hesitate to have seconds.

342
00:19:57,160 --> 00:19:58,160
Y-yeah.

343
00:20:01,420 --> 00:20:02,860
That's strange.

344
00:20:02,860 --> 00:20:05,000
It's like their attitude suddenly changed.

345
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:06,260
Am I imagining things?

346
00:20:06,900 --> 00:20:09,480
W-what?

347
00:20:12,140 --> 00:20:13,900
T-this is what I saw earlier.

348
00:20:13,900 --> 00:20:16,100
But why is it here?

349
00:20:16,100 --> 00:20:17,580
Was that all right, then?

350
00:20:18,720 --> 00:20:20,220
W-why...

351
00:20:21,760 --> 00:20:23,540
Well, no particular reason.

352
00:20:23,540 --> 00:20:24,000
What?

353
00:20:24,940 --> 00:20:26,520
I-I can't believe it.

354
00:20:26,860 --> 00:20:29,520
The Chief buying me something?

355
00:20:29,520 --> 00:20:32,540
And Flora was there too, but...

356
00:20:32,540 --> 00:20:35,320
Want to go in together?

357
00:20:43,560 --> 00:20:44,200
What's wrong?

358
00:20:44,600 --> 00:20:46,100
No, no, it's nothing.

359
00:20:46,800 --> 00:20:48,760
It's strange. Something's definitely off.

360
00:20:48,760 --> 00:20:50,740
Suddenly being this kind to us?

361
00:20:51,980 --> 00:20:54,400
Sorry for being so hard on you.

362
00:20:55,600 --> 00:20:59,360
Looking at you,
I just can't help thinking of Ryotsu.

363
00:21:00,300 --> 00:21:03,380
Ryotsu is one of my subordinates.

364
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:06,360
He's a completely hopeless good-for-nothing.

365
00:21:07,040 --> 00:21:09,080
Your manners are utterly lacking,

366
00:21:09,480 --> 00:21:11,120
and your general attitude is the worst.

367
00:21:11,120 --> 00:21:13,600
If I leave you the way you are,

368
00:21:13,600 --> 00:21:16,440
you'll grow up to be a
hopeless adult like Ryotsu.

369
00:21:16,980 --> 00:21:19,580
That's why I ended up
being so strict with you.

370
00:21:20,940 --> 00:21:22,080
I shouldn't get angry.

371
00:21:22,080 --> 00:21:24,340
I'm not Ryotsu now.

372
00:21:24,340 --> 00:21:25,460
But...

373
00:21:27,960 --> 00:21:30,160
Still, children really are nice.

374
00:21:30,160 --> 00:21:33,540
I have a daughter, but no son.

375
00:21:34,160 --> 00:21:36,500
If I had a lively son like you,

376
00:21:36,500 --> 00:21:39,000
I would have taught him all sorts of things.

377
00:21:40,900 --> 00:21:45,200
I see. So that's what that look meant.

378
00:21:46,040 --> 00:21:48,260
That's why you've been so unusually gentle.

379
00:21:56,780 --> 00:22:00,960
Then there's no reason not to take advantage of this opportunity,
is there?

380
00:22:01,540 --> 00:22:02,660
Hey, mister.

381
00:22:02,660 --> 00:22:04,120
What is it?

382
00:22:04,120 --> 00:22:07,703
Hey, while I'm staying here, can I call you

383
00:22:07,753 --> 00:22:09,900
"Dad"?

384
00:22:10,820 --> 00:22:12,740
You'd like to call me that?

385
00:22:13,920 --> 00:22:15,648
Yeah. And then, Dad,

386
00:22:15,698 --> 00:22:18,160
there's something I've always wanted.

387
00:22:18,160 --> 00:22:21,980
Say whatever you want.
Dad will buy it for you.

388
00:22:21,980 --> 00:22:24,701
Well, first,
a radio-controlled car and a model kit,

389
00:22:24,751 --> 00:22:27,360
then games, a TV, and DVDs,

390
00:22:27,360 --> 00:22:28,020
uh-huh, uh-huh.

391
00:22:29,320 --> 00:22:35,040
And then, a bicycle, an air gun,
and a new cell phone too.

392
00:22:36,480 --> 00:22:38,180
And then, and then...

393
00:22:38,900 --> 00:22:44,760
Right, I want a computer!

394
00:22:44,760 --> 00:22:47,660
Come on, Dad, please, buy them, buy them!

395
00:22:48,560 --> 00:22:50,040
Ryotsu...

396
00:22:50,040 --> 00:22:54,300
What are you saying, Dad?
I'm not Ryotsu or anything!

397
00:22:54,300 --> 00:22:56,040
I'm your son, Dad.

398
00:22:58,680 --> 00:23:01,460
Don't tell me the candy's
effect has worn off?

399
00:23:03,980 --> 00:23:07,320
So that kid was you all along?

400
00:23:08,620 --> 00:23:11,500
Well, you see, there are a lot
of circumstances behind this.

401
00:23:12,060 --> 00:23:12,738
Yes, yes,

402
00:23:12,788 --> 00:23:16,720
It's all because of the
rejuvenating candy Esaki made!

403
00:23:16,900 --> 00:23:18,280
Shut up, you idiot!

404
00:23:19,060 --> 00:23:20,800
Whoa! Mecha!

405
00:23:22,600 --> 00:23:23,600
Whoa, wait, hey!

406
00:23:23,620 --> 00:23:24,720
Stop it!

407
00:23:24,720 --> 00:23:25,940
Hey, okay, be quiet!

408
00:23:36,700 --> 00:23:41,580
Please use this candy properly
and follow the dosage instructions.

409
00:23:41,580 --> 00:23:42,340
Phone call

410
00:24:01,020 --> 00:24:04,560
Sandals any time,
scandals any time, don't mind it

411
00:24:05,460 --> 00:24:09,040
Playing it cool, every day

412
00:24:09,040 --> 00:24:13,960
Boredom's crumpled into
a reprimand and tossed away

413
00:24:15,020 --> 00:24:18,460
Bare instincts, naked instincts,
go wild and be a fool

414
00:24:19,500 --> 00:24:22,180
Reckless and broke, so what's the problem?

415
00:24:22,180 --> 00:24:23,200
That's not it

416
00:24:23,200 --> 00:24:26,620
My way, doing things however I please

417
00:24:26,620 --> 00:24:28,020
That's all there is to it

418
00:24:28,020 --> 00:24:28,760
Amazing

419
00:24:28,760 --> 00:24:30,800
The rigid Chief's thunder

420
00:24:30,800 --> 00:24:32,600
Smoke from the head

421
00:24:33,420 --> 00:24:35,640
Run away and it's a Kame-agari!

422
00:24:35,640 --> 00:24:36,040
Kame-agari!

423
00:24:36,040 --> 00:24:37,380
Well, isn't that wonderful.

424
00:24:37,380 --> 00:24:38,200
Ohoo!

425
00:24:38,200 --> 00:24:39,820
In the flowery Edo,

426
00:24:39,820 --> 00:24:40,500
Yaitoo!

427
00:24:40,500 --> 00:24:41,840
Ryozan Typhoon!

428
00:24:41,840 --> 00:24:42,900
Thanks for your business!

429
00:24:42,900 --> 00:24:45,300
Raging wild!

430
00:24:45,300 --> 00:24:47,520
Workers' Play 9×2!

431
00:24:47,520 --> 00:24:48,980
10 games, 10 games!

432
00:24:48,980 --> 00:24:51,240
Heart too much, bold as fish in water.

433
00:24:52,180 --> 00:24:56,380
Water-going pine, group-going pine, wind-coming
pine, a place to sleep, a place to live.

434
00:24:56,980 --> 00:25:01,020
Snake-village koji, village koji,
Paipo Paipo, Paipo's Shuringan!

435
00:25:01,020 --> 00:25:06,240
Shuringan's Guringdai, Guringdari's
Poppoko-kki's Poppoko, and so on!

436
00:25:06,240 --> 00:25:07,840
Super-investigator Chōsuke!

437
00:25:16,480 --> 00:25:21,420
Festivals are great, aren't they? Hear the word
"festival" and I just can't sit still!

438
00:25:23,440 --> 00:25:24,940
Never mind, it's fine.

439
00:25:25,220 --> 00:25:28,780
Hey, Lemon,
let me teach you how to enjoy a festival.

440
00:25:29,180 --> 00:25:31,820
Next time, memories from the food stalls.
See you then!

